## Context

The tournament produced three diffusable findings: (1) the instrument —
a reusable arena (skills/arena) measuring quality/speed/cost on real
harness tickets; (2) the results — Luna as default workhorse, the local
flash-next beating hosted Sol 6.1 @medium paired 7-2, Sol @low strictly
dominating Sol @medium, Opus @low at parity with @medium at 1/3 cost;
(3) the doctrine — effort levels are model-relative identity traits
(Qwen 3.8 compensates size with duration by default).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Post drafts in French, referencing the report (1046) for figures
- [ ] Egress check: public specs and scores only, no project content
- [ ] Author review and go for publication
